    "details": "<p><strong>ModelWars</strong> is a multi-stage <strong>Machine Learning</strong> competition where models fight, strategies clash, and adaptability is the key to survival. Battle through dataset challenges, token-based decisions, adversarial sabotage, and model explanation rounds to prove your machine learning skills. Teams build a machine learning model that can withstand corrupted data, adapt to missing essential features, and clearly justify the reasoning behind their modelling choices.</p>\n<p><em>Where Models Fight, Minds Win!</em></p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Open to students from all colleges and universities.</li>\n<li><strong>Team Size:</strong> 1 - 3 participants per team.</li>\n<li><strong>Inter-College Teams:</strong> Allowed. Pariticipants from different colleges may form a team.</li>\n<li><strong>Inter-Specialization Teams:</strong> Allowed. Participants from differents branches/specializations may form a team.</li>\n<li><strong>Competition Format:</strong> The competition consists of three rounds:\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>The Dataset Games:</strong> Model development, progressive dataset unlocking, token management, sidequests, and leaderboard competition.</li>\n<li><strong>Model Kombat:</strong> Adversarial dataset sabotage and model adaptation.</li>\n<li><strong>Explainfinity War:</strong> In-person explanation and defence of modelling approaches and decisions.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Dataset Access:</strong> Teams begin with 30% of the dataset and can unlock additional portions progressively: 30% &rarr; 45% &rarr; 70% &rarr; 100%, subject to the required model performance threshold.</li>\n<li><strong>Tokens:</strong> Teams use tokens for private score checks and leaderboard submissions. Additional tokens can be earned through sidequests and bonuses.</li>\n<li><strong>Qualification:</strong> Only the top-ranked teams from Round 1 qualify for Round 2. The highest-ranked teams from Round 2 advance to the final round.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 3 Presentation:</strong> Finalists must explain their modelling approach, justify their decisions and trade-offs, and discuss how they adapted to the sabotage introduced in Round 2.</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> Round 1 - 75 minutes; Round 2 - 75 minutes; Round 3 - 45 minutes.</li>\n<li><strong>Date and Time:</strong> 25th September 2026, 10:00 AM - 2:00 PM.</li>\n<li><strong>Venue:</strong> SNU Chennai, AB3 Lab 14 and Lab 15, Second Floor.</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-09-25T13:45:00+05:30",
